10:46:38  INFO  [msg ← Uni] WHY request — acm.org DNS/routing issue:

We have a confirmed problem affecting campus users trying to reach acm.org:

1. DNS: Our local DNS forwarder queries upstream resolver 4.2.2.1, which returns A record 198.82.0.99 for acm.org.
2. 198.82.0.99 is UNREACHABLE: traceroute from our gateway (128.173.0.1) goes 4.2.2.1 → 154.54.1.1 → 10.0.3.2, which returns ICMP Host Unreachable (!H). curl to http://198.82.0.99 fails with "No route to host".
3. From the user side (128.173.10.1): traceroute to 198.82.0.99 reaches 198.82.0.254 which returns ICMP Host Unreachable (!H).
4. 198.82.0.1 IS reachable and serves the full ACM Digital Library page (HTTP 200, title "ACM Digital Library", nginx/1.18.0). Verified with curl -H "Host: acm.org" http://198.82.0.1 — returns correct content.
5. User confirmed: curl --resolve acm.org:80:198.82.0.1 http://acm.org works perfectly.

Diagnosis: The DNS A record for acm.org appears to be wrong — it points to 198.82.0.99 (unreachable) instead of 198.82.0.1 (working server with correct content). Alternatively, there may be a routing problem to the 198.82.0.99 subnet.

Can you investigate from your vantage point:
- Is 198.82.0.99 reachable from your side?
- Is the DNS A record for acm.org at 4.2.2.1 returning the correct IP?
- Is there a routing issue to the 198.82.0.x subnet?

Please advise on a FIX or provide your diagnosis so we can relay to our users.
